{"title":"Siemens Competition","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Siemens Competition</b> in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Science\" title=\"Science\">science</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Technology\" title=\"Technology\">technology</a> is one of the largest national scholarship competitions in the United States.  Sponsored by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Siemens_Foundation&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Siemens Foundation (page does not exist)\">Siemens Foundation</a>, the top prize is a $100,000 scholarship.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Siemens_Competition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.siemens-foundation.org/\">Siemens Foundation Homepage</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Community/AoPS_Y_MJ_Transcripts.php?mj_id=154\">Siemens Competition informational</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_Jam\" title=\"Math Jam\">Math Jam</a>, including Q&amp;A with 2005 winner Michael Viscardi, a member of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> community.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Siemens_Competition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a 